# Expectation record for 06_control_flow/004_switch_edge_cases.c
#
# Reproduce one cell by hand with no harness: render the three command templates
# below, substituting the target triple, the optimization level, the source path,
# the output path, and the target's runner (empty on the natively executing target).

program            = 004_switch_edge_cases
area               = 06_control_flow
description        = Switch edge cases: empty body, default first, default absent, single label, unordered labels, and the discriminating dense versus sparse label sets that select jump-table versus comparison-chain lowering
targets            = x86_64, i686, aarch64, riscv64
opt_levels         = -O0, -O1, -O2
shared_flags       = -static
bcc_command        = $BCC --target <triple> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
ref_command        = $REF_CC_<TRIPLE> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
run_command        = <runner> <out>
expect_exit        = 0
oracle_a           = enabled
oracle_b           = enabled
oracle_c           = enabled
ub_notes           <<END
Every controlling value is an integer literal, staged through the volatile int
vin in the runtime variant, and every case label is a distinct integer constant
expression. The widest label magnitude is 1000000 and the widest input magnitude
is 1000000, both far inside the range of a 32-bit int on all four targets, so no
signed overflow is possible. The largest accumulated value is 1720, the sum of
the sixteen dense results, which is likewise far inside range. There is no
shift, no division, no remainder and no pointer arithmetic. Every object is
written before it is read: r is assigned on every reachable path in each helper,
and is pre-initialised in empty_body, default_absent and single_label where a
non-matching value runs no arm at all; the static const input tables have
initialisers; vin is assigned before each read; and every out[] element is
written before it is printed, including the two accumulators which are set to
zero before their sweep loops. No object is modified twice between sequence
points; each volatile write and each volatile read stands in its own statement or
its own controlling expression. There is no aliasing, no address is taken, no
uninitialised storage is read, and nothing depends on padding bytes or on the
relative addresses of unrelated objects. No evaluation order is relied upon: the
helper calls appearing together in one printf argument list are pure. The empty
switch body is well formed and executes nothing for any value.
END
impl_defined_notes <<END
Nothing implementation-defined is printed. Plain char is never used as a value,
which matters because char signedness was measured to differ across the four
targets: signed on x86_64 and i686, unsigned on aarch64 and riscv64. Every
printed value has type int, which is 32 bits on all four targets, so no value
depends on the measured pointer and long width difference (4 bytes on i686,
8 bytes on the other three). No address, no pointer value, no sizeof result and
no floating-point value is printed. The choice of switch lowering strategy is
deliberately allowed to differ between targets and between optimization levels:
assembly inspection of the reference compiler at -O0 confirmed that the dense
sixteen-label switch and the biased eight-label switch each lower to a single
indirect jump through a jump table, while the six-label sparse switch lowers to a
comparison chain with no indirect jump at all. That difference is a difference of
generated code, not of observable result, so it is not an implementation-defined
value difference and needs no target restriction. All 12 cells are therefore
expected to produce byte-identical stdout.
END
expected_stdout    <<END
const_empty_body=5 5
runtime_empty_body=5 5
const_default_first=2 3 1
runtime_default_first=2 3 1
const_default_absent=111 122 100
runtime_default_absent=111 122 100
const_single_label=1 0
runtime_single_label=1 0
const_unordered_labels=1 2 3 0
runtime_unordered_labels=1 2 3 0
const_dense=100 101 107 115 999 999
runtime_dense=100 101 107 115 999 999
const_dense_offset=1 5 8 0
runtime_dense_offset=1 5 8 0
const_sparse=1 2 3 4 5 6 0 0
runtime_sparse=1 2 3 4 5 6 0 0
dense_sweep_total=1720
sparse_sweep_total=21
END
